   "definition_quote": "In our model of the Distributed Multi-Armed Bandit problem, there are $k \\ge 1$ individual players. The players are given $n$ arms... Each arm $i \\in [n]$ is associated with a reward, which is a $[0,1]$-valued random variable with expectation $p_i$... In the best-arm identification version of the problem, the goal ... is that with probability at least $1-\\del$ all players correctly identify the best arm."
